# TTS Accessibility & Voice Assistance – MediMind

## 1. Purpose of this document
This document explains how Text-To-Speech (TTS) accessibility is implemented in the MediMind project.

The goal is to:

- Improve accessibility for visually impaired users  
- Allow users to hear medication information  
- Provide spoken summaries of treatments  
- Prevent overlapping voice playback  
- Maintain clean architecture through a centralized TTS service  

This system ensures inclusive design and controlled voice behavior across the entire app.

---

## 2. Technology Used

- flutter_tts package
- Hive (for voice preference persistence)
- Central TTSService (Singleton pattern)

IMPORTANT:
- TTS must NEVER be implemented directly inside screens.
- All voice functionality must go through TTSService.

---

## 3. Architecture Overview

Voice functionality is centralized in:

`lib/core/service/tts_service.dart`

UI triggers speech using:

`TTSService.instance.speak(text)`

To prevent overlapping speech:

`TTSService.instance.stopIfSpeaking()`

---

## 4. Core Design Principles

### Centralized Control
All voice playback is controlled by a single TTSService instance.

### No Overlapping Audio
Before navigating screens or starting new speech:
- stopIfSpeaking() is called
- dispose() methods stop active speech

### Screen Lifecycle Safety
Each major screen includes:

@override
void dispose() {
TTSService.instance.stopIfSpeaking();
super.dispose();
}



This prevents background audio when navigating.

---

## 5. Voice Integration by Screen

### Home Screen
- Each dose has a volume icon
- Speaks:
  "Medication scheduled at HH:MM."

### Schedule Screen
- AppBar voice icon
- Generates dynamic summary:
  - Number of active medications
  - Dosage
  - Intake times
  - Low stock warnings

### Medical ID Screen
- Speaks full medical summary:
  - Blood type
  - Allergies
  - Emergency contact

### Medications (Cabinet)
- Speaks:
  - Number of medications
  - Dosage
  - Current stock levels

### Privacy Screen
- Speaks:
  - Privacy overview
  - Policy details
  - GDPR rights explanations
- Dialog popups include SpeakerButton

### Main Screen (Bottom Navigation)
- Automatically stops speech when switching tabs

void _onItemTapped(int index) {
TTSService.instance.stopIfSpeaking();
setState(() {
_selectedIndex = index;
});
}


